Find the length $x$, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.5,4.3301);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$x$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=1.5,"$60^{\circ}$"] {angle=B--A--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A triangular paddock has two sides of lengths $180$ m and $120$ m, with an included angle of $120^{\circ}$. Find the third side, correct to the nearest metre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (-1.5,2.5981);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$180\text{ m}$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,left] {$120\text{ m}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$x$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=1.5,"$120^{\circ}$"] {angle=B--A--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the perimeter of the triangle, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (G) at (0,0);
\coordinate (H) at (3.6,0);
\coordinate (J) at (2.4,4.1569);
\draw (G)--(H)--(J)--cycle;
\path (G)--(H) node[midway,below] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (G)--(J) node[midway,above left] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=1.5,"$60^{\circ}$"] {angle=H--G--J};
\node[below left] at (G) {$G$};
\node[below right] at (H) {$H$};
\node[above] at (J) {$J$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
